  <infoLinks>
    <infoLink name="And They Shall Know No Fear" id="8096-77ac-a426-958a" hidden="false" targetId="73f8-658e-9da5-beba" type="rule"/>
  </infoLinks>
  <rules>
    <rule name="Righteous Zeal" id="6030-5e6b-3b4d-4eb3" hidden="false">
      <description>In the Shooting phase, any Infantry unit (not Jump Infantry) that is not Pinned or Falling Back must take a Morale check if it suffers any casualties from enemy shooting, not just when it suffers 25&quot; casualties. All other units in the Black Templars army check Morale and fall back as normal. Note that all Black Templars units take Pinning tests as normal.


If an Infantry unit (including any attached characters) is called upon to make a Morale check and passes it, then the unit must move towards the nearest visible enemy unit. This is identical to a Consolidate move that has been achieved from destroying an enemy unit in close combat. Should the unit fail this Morale check, it will fall back as normal.


Black Templars who are Tank Shocked and pass their test do not benefit from Righteous Zeal.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Abhor the Witch" id="d417-6048-a0fb-7a4c" hidden="false">
      <description>No models with Psychic powers may be fielded as an ally to the Black Templars and they will not fight as allies to any army that includes any models with Psychic powers, with the exception of Grey Knight Space Marines.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="No Pity! No Remorse! No Fear!" id="bf0b-8658-ac74-5b47" hidden="false">
      <description>When in an assault, all Black Templar units are Fearless.</description>
    </rule>
  </rules>
